//! The `letter-spacing` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property sets the
//! spacing between text characters. This value is added to the natural spacing between characters
//! while rendering the text. Positive values of `letter-spacing` spread characters further apart,
//! while negative values of `letter-spacing` bring characters closer together.
//!
//! Initial: normal. Inherited: yes.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Grammar: normal | <length-percentage>
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-text-4/#propdef-letter-spacing
//!
//! Author guide:
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/letter-spacing
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

